// @@@ If the index is between 0 and the size of the list inclusive, then for every valid index i less than the specified index, either the element at i is null and was null before, or it remains unchanged from its previous state.
--------------------
// @@@ If the index is valid (between 0 and the size of the list, inclusive), then for every index i from 0 to just before the specified index, the element at position i in the list remains unchanged or continues to be null after the operation.
